// Granted onto a target by DamageUtility.TryMarkExplodeOnDeath whenever it's hit by an owner holding
// MarkExplosiveDeath (Max's Berserk upgrade, Pixie's bomb upgrade - same shared grant, doesn't matter
// which one marked it). Presence means "explode when this thing dies" - see
// DamageUtility.TryExplodeOnDeath, checked in the enemy-death branch of ApplyDamage.
//
// Permanent - once marked, an enemy stays Unstable until it dies (there used to be a Remaining
// countdown + ExplodeOnDeathTimerSystem that "cured" it; removed 2026-10-21).
//
// Killer is only set once the marked enemy actually dies: instead of exploding on the spot, it's parked in
// EnemyActionPhase.Dead for ExplodeOnDeathConfig.DetonationDelay (the view shakes it - "fuse") and then
// detonates from EnemySystem.UpdateDead via DamageUtility.DetonateExplodeOnDeathFuse, credited to Killer.
// A short fuse per corpse is what keeps a kill + its chain blasts readable as separate beats.
component ExplodeOnDeath
{
    EntityRef Killer;
}
